- WRG | keep it one stall, and keep the Saturdays for the joy of it | habit | v: hedonism, tradition | tribal: keep it one fire, and bake for the joy of it | magic: keep it one stall, and keep the market days for the joy of it | foot: means freedom+.05 | chance: 84
- WBR | sell the recipe to a big chain for a fair price and a share | grants: savings | v: power, security | tribal: trade the way of the cakes to the great band, for goods now and a share later | magic: sell the recipe to a great house for a fair price and a share | chance: 84
- UBR | take an evening course in running a business while the stall keeps going | grants: bookkeeping | self_control: + | v: achievement, self-direction | tribal: sit with an old trader through the winter, and learn how a trade is carried | magic: take lessons from a guild clerk in the evenings while the stall keeps going | foot: place learn.higher | chance: 84
- UBG | ask the investor for a smaller sum, and a mentor from their firm | grants: mentor | v: achievement, benevolence | tribal: ask the great band's trader for a little, and to teach you the trade | magic: ask the backer for a smaller sum, and a mentor from the merchant house | chance: 84
works: Within a year the thing {N} started is sold in three places at once, and the first stall still has its queue.
works: Whatever {N} chose, the baking goes on, and {N} is glad of the road taken.
fails: The money comes with terms nobody could meet, and by the winter it is one stall again.
