# ================================================================ world-only

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 9. a seat among the merchant princes (only: magic; pairs D1a)
# The magic crossing to the summit: a seat on the council of merchant princes falls free, and whoever wins the vote is
# named a merchant prince ([magnate], the facet on the guild master's or the merchant's career). Four singles try for
# it plainly at its real chance, 6. White's way is the old bargain: the founder's oath sworn in the vault under the
# counting-house to the old thing that keeps the guild's ledgers, which turns votes for a price named later (someone
# else's power, never the person's own gift; anyone may swear it), at 16, with the Order's disapproval on a closed:
# approval line and its backfire (it comes to collect). It is White's because it is an oath and a rite, the guild's
# oldest, kept to the letter. The pairs are the season's honest other roads: an old friend backed for the seat ([friend
# in power]), the dead prince's ships bought at the auction ([shares]), a year spent learning the council, a speech
# against seats bought and sold, the council's clerkship. They form a ring (each colour in two), so their chances are
# solved around the singles (WR, WU and BG at 65; UG and BR at 85) until every colour's mean is 40.5. The gate
# (LIFE_CALLINGS) asks for three years as guild master or six as merchant.

== a seat among the merchant princes
tier: life event
only: magic
stages: adult mature elder
age: 30-100
holds: chief executive | founder of a firm
tenure: 3-99
per_year: 0 0 0 .02 .02 .01
drivers: prosper+.2 fortune+.2
times: per guild master or merchant with a house of their own, of three years or more, in the magic world a year: about 1 in 60 see a seat on the council of merchant princes fall free while they could stand for it (estimate); the council's seats are few and held for life, and the merchant princes are about 5 lives in 100,000 (catalogue share for the magnate; estimate)
likelier: a house that has traded well for years, backers among the great houses, a prince who owes the house a favour
rarer: a lean year at sea, a house far from the capital's port, an old feud with a prince's family
gap: 8-15
tone: joy
life: work, money, publiclife
horizon: months
roles: rival, mentor, friend, boss
magic: a seat on the council of merchant princes falls free, and the princes vote at the new moon
scene magic: The oldest of the merchant princes, who held the spice wharves for fifty years, has died, and his seat on the council falls free. The princes will vote at the new moon, and {rival} is already sending gifts. In the cellars under the old counting-house, the merchants whisper, something older than the city keeps a ledger of every debt, and will turn a vote for a price it names later.
scene magic W: The council's charter is four hundred years old, and every word of it still binds. Its oldest page, {N} knows, speaks of an oath the founders swore in the vault below.
scene magic U: The princes' votes each have a reason. {N} has started a chart of who owes whom, who fears whom and who hates whom.
scene magic B: A seat among the princes is a share of the realm's trade for life, and a name the king's treasurer knows. {N} has wanted it since the first ship came home.
scene magic R: {N} would rather win the seat at the council table, face to face, than by a hundred whispers in a hundred corridors.
scene magic G: {Ns} house has traded on the old coast road for four generations. {N} thinks of the families along it, and what a seat on the council would mean for them.
- W | go down to the old vault, and swear the founder's oath to what keeps the ledgers | title: magnate | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: a bargain sworn with the old thing under the counting-house, without the Order's leave; backfire: it comes to collect, and takes the house's luck and the seat with it | binds | self_control: - | v: tradition, power | chance: 16
- U | chart who owes whom, and win each prince with what that prince wants | title: magnate | v: achievement, power | chance: 6
- B | call in every debt the princes owe the house, one by one, before the vote | title: magnate | aims: magnate | v: power | chance: 6
- R | stand up at the council table, and ask for the seat face to face | title: magnate | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 6
- G | bring the families of the coast road to the guildhall to speak for the house | title: magnate | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 6
- BG | back an old friend for the seat, and ask a share of the trade in return | grants: friend in power | v: power, tradition | chance: 65
- BR | buy the dead prince's ships at the auction, while the others argue | grants: shares | v: power, stimulation | chance: 85
- UG | wait a year, learn how the council votes, and stand next time | mark: learned a skill | self_control: + | v: achievement, security | chance: 85
- WR | speak at the guildhall against seats bought and sold, whoever wins | v: universalism, conformity | foot: place rule.voice | chance: 65
- WU | ask for the council's clerkship instead, and learn its votes from the inside | grants: inner circle at work | v: achievement, security | chance: 65
works: At the new moon the princes vote, and {N} takes the empty chair at the council table.
works: Whatever {N} chose, the season of the vote is remembered well, and the house's name is spoken in the great halls.
fails: The princes choose another house, and {N} is thanked by the council's clerk and shown down the long stair.
fails: The vote is put off a year, the seat goes to a prince's nephew, and the house is no nearer the table.
